window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b><i>Something is wrong with the dead in Inferno . . . it's time to call the professionals.</i></b><br> <br> <b><i>Death magic meets fae attitude in this sexy new PNR, perfect for fans of K F Breene and Linsey Hall who love their stories with a side of sassy ghosts, demi-gods, and necromantic chaos.</i></b><br> <br> Tareal Vanth, a demi-fae necromancer, was having a regular day of cleaning up bodies, taking out murdering trash, and pissing off local authorities . . . he should have known that peace and quiet wouldn't last in a city like Inferno.<br> <br> Now, an actual Reaper called Elektra is on his doorstep, demanding his help to stop a renegade necromancer from tearing the Veil apart and unleashing an undead army.<br> <br> He wants to tell her that it's not his problem, but Elektra's death magic sings to him like a siren song, and his fae mating instincts are getting more frustrated by the second.<br> <br> They are going to need more than the usual tricks to figure out where the rogue necromancer is hiding, even if that means going to disreputable magicians, lost family members, and the dragons themselves to demand they get off their golden asses to save their city. What could possibly go wrong?<br> <br> Contains mature themes.</p>"; 
